  "macroTheme": "Markets enter the most important week of Q3: Fed poised to deliver +25bp hike to 3.75-4.00% (86% probability) following hot August CPI (3.4% YoY). Brent crude surged above $100 to $104.61 on Gulf shipping disruptions. US 10Y yields briefly touched 4.99%. ECB already delivered +25bp. The question has shifted from 'when will rates fall' to 'how much further will they rise.' Warsh press conference Wednesday is the paramount event for all instruments.",
  "macroOverview": "Risk-off tone dominates as oil above $100 and bond yields near 5% converge with a live Fed hike. US30 closed below critical 53,143 support. NAS100 consolidates 28,500-30,000 range. GER40 collapsed -4.7% from ATH on ECB hike and energy shock. Gold correction extends to -21.1% from Iran-war high. UK gilt crisis escalates with 30Y yields approaching 6%. BoE and BoJ also meet this week alongside the Fed. The CPI print Friday cemented the hike but equities bounced on the 'bad news is priced' dynamic.",
